        			</tr>
        		</table>
        		<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript">
        	function checkChildren(srcObj, vType) {
        		for (var i = 0; i < eval("document.formSMC." + vType + ".length"); i++) {
        			if ((eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].value.substring(0, srcObj.length)") == srcObj) && (eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].disabled") == false)) {
        					(eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].checked")) ? eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = false : eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = true;
        			}
        		}
        		return false;
        	}
        function toggleRepealed(element) {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        		else {
        			row.classList.remove('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        function HideRepealed() {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        </script>
        <div style="padding: 15px;"><form action="/smc/" method="post" name="formSMC">
        <div id="hideRepealed">
        		<p><a href="/smc/?Title=13">Title 13</a> Public Utilities and Services</p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=13.02">Chapter 13.02</a> Solid Waste</p>
        						<p>Article VI. Disposal Rates</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0572">Section 13.02.0572</a> Weight Slips<br />
        <p>A three-dollar administrative time charge per weight slip in a disposal transaction is assessed for a second copy.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>						<p>Article VII. Additional Provisions</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0600">Section 13.02.0600</a> Repeal and Savings<br />
        <p>The adoption of this chapter repeals the previously existing <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=13.02">chapter 13.02 SMC</a>, provided that any amendment, repeal, modification or revision of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=13.02">chapter 13.02 SMC</a> shall not be construed to affect any existing right acquired under provisions amended, repealed, modified or revised, or acquired under any rules, regulations or orders issued or adopted pursuant to the authority of this chapter, or as affecting any proceedings instituted thereunder.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0605">Section 13.02.0605</a> No Special Duty<br />
        <p>This chapter creates and the City shall have no special duty to any person or class. Any duty nonetheless deemed to exist shall be a duty to the general public as a whole, and not to any specific person or class.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0610">Section 13.02.0610</a> Penalty<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Except where otherwise specified for violations of this chapter relating to single-family residence service, violations are a civil infraction with each day a new and separate violation. All infraction penalties are in addition to actual costs of clean-up or other services provided by the City.</span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 24, 2025</p><p>ORD C36702 Section 39</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0615">Section 13.02.0615</a> Provisions Supplemental – Preemption<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>A variety of federal, state and local laws regulate storage, collection, handling and disposal of specialized wastes and materials hazardous to the public health.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The provisions of this chapter are supplemental to any other jurisdictional laws or regulations.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>In event of conflict, the most restrictive provisions apply.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>In case of preemption, any preempted provisions shall be considered as if not enacted with respect to the specific circumstances in which the preemption arises.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.02.0620">Section 13.02.0620</a> Severability<br />
        <p>If any section, subdivision, part or word of this chapter or any regulation, rule or order adopted pursuant to the authority thereof be determined invalid, it shall not affect the remainder, but be confined to the section, subdivision, part or word directly involved in the controversy.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=13.03">Chapter 13.03</a> Sewers</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0000">Section 13.03.0000</a> Title<br />
        <p>This chapter may also be referred to as the “sewer code.”</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.1006">Section 13.03.1006</a> REPEALED (User Charge – Standard Strength Wastewater – Monthly Amount)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C36586</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, January 1, 2025</p><p>ORD C36586 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.1014">Section 13.03.1014</a> REPEALED (Service Outside City Utility Service Area – Monthly Amount)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2020</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2021</p><p>ORD C35962 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.1016">Section 13.03.1016</a> REPEALED (Non-domestic Process Wastewater User Charge – Monthly Amount)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2020</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2021</p><p>ORD C35962 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.1226">Section 13.03.1226</a> Water—Wastewater Capital Rates<br />
        <p>
        	Rates for water-wastewater capital are established and provided for in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.035.500" target="_blank">SMC 13.035.500</a>.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 31, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, January 1, 2018</p><p>ORD C35528 Section 11</p>						<p>Article I. Definitions</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0100">Section 13.03.0100</a> Definitions<br />
        <p>The following definitions are derived from the City of Spokane sewer code, originally codified and adopted as <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=13">Title 13 SMC</a> by Ordinance C26294, passed October 12, 1981, as amended. The prior version of this chapter was a recodification passed October 15, 2007, as Ordinance C34122, as amended. These definitions apply to the entire chapter unless otherwise stated or clearly indicated from the context.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 4</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0101">Section 13.03.0101</a> Abbreviations<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">FOG &ndash; Fats, oil, and grease.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0103">Section 13.03.0103</a> REPEALED (“Act”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0105">Section 13.03.0105</a> REPEALED (“Applicable Pretreatment Standard”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0107">Section 13.03.0107</a> REPEALED (“Approval Authority”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0109">Section 13.03.0109</a> REPEALED (“Authorized Representative of the User”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0111">Section 13.03.0111</a> “B.O.D.”<br />
        <p>“B.O.D.”, denoting biochemical oxygen demand, is the quantity of oxygen utilized in the biochemical oxidation of organic matter under standard laboratory procedure in five days at twenty degrees Centigrade, expressed in parts per million by weight.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0113">Section 13.03.0113</a> “Building Drain”<br />
        <p>“Building drain” is that part of the lowest piping of a drainage system which receives the discharge from piping inside the walls of a structure or building to a point two feet outside the outer face of a structure, wall or foundation and conveys it to the sewer or to an on-site sewage disposal system.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0115">Section 13.03.0115</a> REPEALED (“Categorical Pretreatment Standard” or “Categorical Standard”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0117">Section 13.03.0117</a> “Combined Sewer”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Combined sewer&rdquo; is a sewer which conveys any category of wastewater, as permitted by the Wastewater Director, and performs the functions for both a sanitary sewer and a storm sewer.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 7</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0119">Section 13.03.0119</a> REPEALED (“Composite Sample”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0121">Section 13.03.0121</a> “Director” or “POTW Director”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Director&rdquo; or &ldquo;POTW director&rdquo; means the administrative head of the City Wastewater Management Department.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 8</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0123">Section 13.03.0123</a> REPEALED (“Discharge” – Direct, Indirect)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0125">Section 13.03.0125</a> REPEALED (“Grab Sample”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0126">Section 13.03.0126</a> Grease<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&quot;Grease&quot; means liquid or other waste containing floatable and/or dispersed grease, vegetable oil, petroleum oil, non-biodegradable cutting oil, fat, oil or grease products of animal, or vegetable or mineral origin which is detectable and measurable in wastewater.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Thursday, November 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, December 20, 2024</p><p>ORD C36602 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0127">Section 13.03.0127</a> “Industrial Process Wastewater” or “Process Wastewater”<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Industrial process wastewater&rdquo; or &ldquo;process wastewater&rdquo;, also sometimes referred to as &ldquo;non-domestic sewage&rdquo; or by similar terms, is that category of wastewater containing water-carried wastes other than that traditionally derived from human or household customer sources. The term is distinguished from other categories or wastewater identified in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0215"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0215(A)</span></a>.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The term includes two subcategories:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Manufacturing process wastewater&rdquo; is wastewater of a nature, concentration or constituency traditionally originating from industrial or manufacturing customers.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This generally includes sewage from one or more heavy industrial or manufacturing process sources or industrial clean-up procedures.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It includes one process discharge or several commingled process discharges.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Non-manufacturing process wastewater&rdquo; includes all other process wastewater.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This generally includes wastewater from business, institutional or commercial customers which generate non-domestic wastewater components derived from a business or commercial process other than manufacturing or heavy industry.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Examples of included sources are wastewater from commercial laundries, radiator shops and photo finishers, as well as wastewater from vehicles used for storage or transportation of wastewater, such as septic tank pumpers or haulers.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0129">Section 13.03.0129</a> REPEALED (“Interference”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0131">Section 13.03.0131</a> “Lateral” or “Lateral Sewer”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Lateral&rdquo; or &ldquo;lateral sewer&rdquo; is a sewer to which side or private sewers may be connected from adjacent or vicinal properties.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The service area for a lateral is determined by the Wastewater Director based upon generally accepted engineering practices and subject to Spokane municipal practice.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 8</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0133">Section 13.03.0133</a> “Lower Explosive Limit”<br />
        <p>“Lower explosive limit” is the lowest concentration of a gas-in-air mixture at which a gas can ignite.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0137">Section 13.03.0137</a> REPEALED (“National Pretreatment Standards”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0139">Section 13.03.0139</a> “Natural Outlet”<br />
        <p>“Natural outlet” is any outlet into a watercourse, pond, ditch, lake or other body of surface water or groundwater. It does not include connections to the City of Spokane POTW, authorized on-site sewage or stormwater disposal systems, or other authorized sewage disposal mechanisms or systems.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0141">Section 13.03.0141</a> REPEALED (“New Source” – “New User”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0143">Section 13.03.0143</a> “Noncontact Cooling Water”<br />
        <p>“Noncontact cooling water” is that category of wastewater consisting of water used for cooling, generally in an industrial or manufacturing process, which does not come into direct contact with any raw material, intermediate product, waste product or finished product. The term excludes other categories of wastewater identified in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0215">SMC 13.03.0215(A)</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0145">Section 13.03.0145</a> “Non-standard Strength Sewage”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Non-standard strength sewage&rdquo; is wastewater accepted for discharge into the POTW but which does not meet the criteria for acceptance as standard strength sewage, whether because of special characteristics, special treatment requirements, special monitoring or additional handling as a condition of acceptance.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Specific criteria defining this class of wastewater are determined by the Wastewater Director, in the exercise of sound discretion, considering the purposes set forth in this chapter, the public health, safety and welfare, and cost and expense to the POTW.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Wastewater Director may further consider average concentrations of total suspended solids, B.O.D. and phosphorus, or other factors and may include any wastewater determined to have any of the following characteristics:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Containing more than three hundred milligrams per liter of suspended solids (TSS); or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Containing more than three hundred milligrams per liter of biochemical oxygen demand (B.O.D.); or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Any other non-standard strength sewage, as defined by statute, ordinance, regulation or the Wastewater Director&rsquo;s order.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 9</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0147">Section 13.03.0147</a> “NPDES”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;NPDES&rdquo; refers to the National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System permit program administered by the State of Washington Department of Ecology.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 11</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0149">Section 13.03.0149</a> “On-site Sewage Disposal System”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;On-site sewage disposal system&rdquo; is any system or combination of piping, treatment or other facilities that store, treat and/or dispose of sewage and effluent on the property where it originates, or an adjacent or nearby property under the ownership of the user of the system or in which the user has a recorded interest for the purpose of maintaining the system on such other property. In general this includes septic tanks and/or cesspools.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 12</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0151">Section 13.03.0151</a> REPEALED (“Pass-through”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0153">Section 13.03.0153</a> “pH”<br />
        <p>“pH” is the negative logarithm of the hydrogen ion concentration.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0155">Section 13.03.0155</a> REPEALED (“Pollutant”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0157">Section 13.03.0157</a> REPEALED (“POTW”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0159">Section 13.03.0159</a> REPEALED (“Pretreatment”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0161">Section 13.03.0161</a> REPEALED (“Pretreatment Program”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0163">Section 13.03.0163</a> REPEALED (“Pretreatment Requirements”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0165">Section 13.03.0165</a> REPEALED (“Pretreatment Standard” or “Standard”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0167">Section 13.03.0167</a> “Private Pump Station”<br />
        <p>“Private pump station” is an appurtenance of a side sewer, private sewer or on-site sewage disposal system which, alone or conjunction with the side sewer or private sewer, conveys standard strength sewage or effluent by lifting or pumping to another sewer.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0169">Section 13.03.0169</a> “Private Sewer”<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li>
        	<p>&ldquo;Private sewer&rdquo; is a sewer:</p>
        
        	<ol>
        		<li>
        		<p>not controlled or maintained by a public authority;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>serving two or more buildings, residences or properties;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>constructed by private contract.<br />
        		&nbsp;</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>In general a private sewer differs from a side sewer in that it serves more than one building or structure.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0171">Section 13.03.0171</a> “Private Storm Sewer”<br />
        <p>“Private storm sewer” is a storm sewer not controlled or maintained by a public authority or connected to a public sewer or discharged into a natural outlet.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0173">Section 13.03.0173</a> REPEALED (“Prohibited Discharge Standards” or “Prohibited Discharges”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0175">Section 13.03.0175</a> “Public Sewer”<br />
        <p>“Public sewer” is a sewer which is controlled and maintained by a public authority. The term includes any publicly controlled and maintained sanitary or other storm or combined sewer.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0177">Section 13.03.0177</a> “Sanitary Sewage”<br />
        <p>“Sanitary sewage”, also sometimes referred to as “domestic sewage”, is that category of wastewater consisting of water-carried wastes from human and household customer sources. The term also includes water-carried wastes from some business, institutional and commercial customers which do not generate wastewater components derived from an industrial or commercial process, as distinguished in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0127">SMC 13.03.0127</a>. The term is distinguished from other categories of wastewater identified in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0215">SMC 13.03.0215(A)</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0179">Section 13.03.0179</a> “Sanitary Sewer”<br />
        <p>“Sanitary sewer” is a sewer which conveys sanitary sewage. Additionally, the term is used to mean any public sewer except a storm sewer.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0181">Section 13.03.0181</a> “Sewage”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Sewage&rdquo; is a combination of the water-carried wastes from domestic, business or commercial, industrial or manufacturing sources, including residences, business buildings, institutions and industrial establishments. &ldquo;Sewage&rdquo; also includes surface water and stormwater when discharged into a sewer system.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 13</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0183">Section 13.03.0183</a> “Sewer System”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Sewer system&rdquo; is a pipe, conduit, structure or appurtenance for conveying sewage. These definitions further identify this term according to who owns or maintains the sewer:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">private sewer,</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">private storm sewer,</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">side sewer,</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">special side sewer,</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">as opposed to public sewer.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In general, public sewers are also subdivided according to what they convey:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">sanitary sewer,</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">storm sewer, and</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">combined sewer.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 14</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0185">Section 13.03.0185</a> “Wastewater Maintenance Superintendent”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Wastewater Maintenance Superintendent&rdquo; is a City official who reports to the Wastewater Director and is responsible for inspecting the work of crews engaged in public sewer construction activity, including extensions, repairs, maintenance and new construction.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This person oversees repair, maintenance and cleaning operations for public sewers.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This person also regulates construction, use and maintenance of publicly-owned catch basins and drains.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This person inspects on-site sewage disposal systems in coordination with the Health Officer.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 15</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0187">Section 13.03.0187</a> “Side Sewer”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Side sewer&rdquo; is a sewer, not directly controlled or maintained by a public authority, which begins two feet outside the outer face of a structure wall or foundation, conveying wastewater from the building drain to the outside annular surface of a public sewer or private sewer, including in the right-of-way</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 16</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0189">Section 13.03.0189</a> “Side Sewer Stub”<br />
        <p>“Side sewer stub” is that portion of a side sewer, constructed along with the public sewer, prior to direct connection to the premises to be served.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0191">Section 13.03.0191</a> REPEALED (“Significant Industrial User”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0193">Section 13.03.0193</a> REPEALED (“Slugload”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0195">Section 13.03.0195</a> “Special Side Sewer”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Special side sewer&rdquo; is a side sewer connected to a lateral or other public or private sewer which is outside the normal service area of said sewer, as determined by the Wastewater Director in the exercise of sound discretion.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="color:black">Unless otherwise indicated or required by the context, all side sewer requirements apply to special side sewers.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 17</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0197">Section 13.03.0197</a> “Standard Strength Sewage”<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Standard strength sewage&rdquo; is wastewater which complies with specifications designated by the Wastewater Director, City sewer rates and regulations, or this code as not requiring special treatment, monitoring or additional handling prior to acceptance by the POTW, considering chemical, physical and organic content, including but not limited to, B.O.D., suspended solids and phosphorus.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Wastewater Director adjusts the definition of &ldquo;standard strength sewage&rdquo; in the City sewer rates resolution.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 18</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0199">Section 13.03.0199</a> “Stormwater”<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>“Stormwater” is that category of wastewater consisting of flows occurring during or following any form of natural precipitation, and resulting from such precipitation, including snowmelt.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The term is distinguished from other categories of wastewater identified in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0215">SMC 13.03.0215(A)</a>.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0201">Section 13.03.0201</a> “Storm Sewer” or “Storm Drain”<br />
        <p>“Storm sewer” or “storm drain” is a sewer which conveys stormwater.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0203">Section 13.03.0203</a> “Suspended Solids”<br />
        <p>“Suspended solids” means the total suspended matter that floats on the surface of or is suspended in water, wastewater or other liquid and which is removable by laboratory filtering.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0205">Section 13.03.0205</a> “System of Sewerage”<br />
        <p>“System of sewerage” is the system of sewers, outfalls, works, plants and facilities for wastewater collection, treatment and disposal, or any and all such facilities of the City used or dedicated to provide public sewer service.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0207">Section 13.03.0207</a> “Total Solids”<br />
        <p>“Total solids” means all matter that can be removed by total evaporation as contained in the manual of “Standard Methods” under total residue.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0209">Section 13.03.0209</a> REPEALED (“Twenty-four Hour Flow-proportional Composite Sample”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0211">Section 13.03.0211</a> REPEALED (“Upset”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0213">Section 13.03.0213</a> REPEALED (“User” or “Industrial User”)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0215">Section 13.03.0215</a> “Wastewater”<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Wastewater&rdquo; includes anything released into the POTW and generally includes water-carried wastes from domestic, business or commercial, or manufacturing or industrial sources.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">For purposes of reference, four categories of wastewater, based on its generic source, are identified in usage:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Sanitary sewage, as defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0177"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0177</span></a>;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Stormwater, defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0199"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0199</span></a>;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Industrial process wastewater or process wastewater, defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0127"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0127</span></a>; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Noncontact cooling water, defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0143"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0143</span></a>.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Additionally, &ldquo;wastewater&rdquo; is divided into two general classes for purposes of rates and treatment requirements:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Standard strength sewage, defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0197"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0197</span></a>; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Non-standard strength sewage, defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0145"><span style="color:blue">SMC 13.03.0145</span></a>.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0216">Section 13.03.0216</a> Grease Control Device(s)<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&quot;Grease control device(s)&quot; means an appurtenance or appliance that is installed in a sanitary drainage system to intercept non-petroleum fats, oil, and grease (FOG) from wastewater. There are three types of grease control devices: gravity grease interceptors, hydromechanical grease interceptors, and mechanical grease removal devices.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0217">Section 13.03.0217</a> Grease Interceptor<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&quot;Grease interceptor&quot; means a large tank installed underground designed to collect and control solid- food wastes and floating grease from wastewater prior to discharge into the sanitary sewer collection system. Grease interceptors are normally installed outside the building and use gravity to separate grease from the wastewater as it moves from one compartment of the interceptor to the next.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 3</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0218">Section 13.03.0218</a> Hydromechanical Grease Interceptor<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Hydromechanical grease interceptor&rdquo; or &quot;grease trap&quot; means a device placed under or in close proximity to sinks or other fixtures likely to discharge grease in an attempt to separate, trap and hold oil and grease substances, prior to discharge into the sanitary sewer collection system.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 4</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0219">Section 13.03.0219</a> Mechanical Grease Removal Device.<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&quot;Mechanical grease removal device&quot; means a power operated device or combination of devices using electrical equipment to heat, filter, siphon, skim or otherwise separate and retain floating grease and solid food waste prior to the wastewater exiting the trap and entering the sanitary sewer collection system.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0220">Section 13.03.0220</a> Oil/Water Separator.<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Oil/water separator&rdquo; means an appurtenance or appliance that is installed in a sanitary sewer drainage system to intercept petroleum fats, oils, and grease (FOG) from wastewater. There are two types of oil/water separators: baffle type separators and coalescing plate separators. </span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 6</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0221">Section 13.03.0221</a> Sand Trap.<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Sand trap&rdquo; means an appurtenance or appliance that is installed in conjunction with an oil/water separator to intercept settleable granular particles from wastewater.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 7</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0222">Section 13.03.0222</a> Septic Tank.<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&quot;Septic tank&quot; means a watertight treatment receptacle receiving the discharge of sewage from a building sewer or sewers, designed and constructed to permit separation of settleable and floating solids from the liquid, and detention and anaerobic digestion of the organic matter, as part of an on-site disposal system. </span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 28, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, October 5, 2023</p><p>ORD C36429 Section 8</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0223">Section 13.03.0223</a> Wastewater Hauler.<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Wastewater hauler&rdquo; is a firm permitted to collect and transport materials removed from onsite grease control devices or septic tanks that may be discharged to a local POTW or discharged to a rendering facility. The Wastewater Director may approve industrial waste on a case-by-case basis.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 19</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0225">Section 13.03.0225</a> Yellow Grease<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&quot;Yellow grease&quot; means grease, which is associated with food preparation or processing that has not been contaminated with wash water or chemicals. Common examples include used cooking and fryer oils.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Thursday, November 14, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, December 20, 2024</p><p>ORD C36602 Section 2</p>						<p>Article III. General Requirements</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0302">Section 13.03.0302</a> Mandatory Sewer Service – No Rights Created – Charge to Unconnected, Occupied Property<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No wastewater, except stormwater, subject to applicable stormwater requirements, may be directly discharged into a natural outlet within the City of Spokane. All wastewater, sewage, wastes and waters, except stormwater, must be discharged into the POTW of the City of Spokane and/or into authorized on-site sewage disposal systems. This obligation applies to the owner of premises and to persons in possession, charge or control of the premises where prohibited discharges either originate or occur.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">This chapter does not create rights for any individual or group to require construction of public sewers, connection thereto, or otherwise to receive sewer service from the City. The City reserves all rights to deny, limit or curtail service.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Charge to Unconnected, Occupied Property.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The City Council finds that the City is within a sole-source aquifer area. On-site sewage systems serving occupied premises should be discouraged to avoid degradation of the aquifer.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Occupied property derives a substantial benefit from the immediate availability of public sewer service, in addition to benefits from specific charges such as a general facilities charge or local improvement district assessments.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">On-site sewage systems tend to delay the installation of sewer lines. Because sewers are the deepest utility in underground location, where sewer lines are delayed as an area continues to develop, a substantially greater expense arises to put in sewer lines beneath other utilities and fixtures which have been installed and paved.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The charge for nonconnection of occupied premises to a public sewer where service is available shall be the rate assessed for such sewer service, except where prohibited by law.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">For purposes of this section, service &ldquo;availability&rdquo; is determined by the Wastewater Director, consistent with this chapter.</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 20</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0304">Section 13.03.0304</a> On-site Sewage Disposal Systems – Policy to Limit<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">It is the policy and intent of the City of Spokane, Spokane County Spokane Regional Health District and various other agencies of the State and Federal governments that on-site sewage disposal be limited and discouraged and, except where specifically authorized by permit, prohibited in all areas, and that all sewage be discharged into the POTW.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No on-site sewage disposal system may be constructed, used or maintained in the City of Spokane without a written permit from the Health Officer certifying that it meets the requirements of the Health District.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">On-site sewage disposal systems must also meet the requirements of the Wastewater Director and this code.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">An on-site sewage disposal system is not permitted whenever:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">public sewer service is available, as defined in subsection (D) of this section; or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">the premises are occupied by a significant industrial user; or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">public health or safety would be adversely affected.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Availability of Public Sewer Service.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">For purposes of this section, except as provided in subsection (D)(2) of this section, public sewer service is available if a street, highway, alley or easement in which a public sewer is located runs within two hundred feet or less at any point from the boundaries of the premises concerned and said premises are located within the design area for the public sewer.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Availability may be deferred from the time public sewer service is located within two hundred feet or less of the property concerned, so long as:</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">sewage disposal service needs are limited to existing residential uses or equivalent, but this does not extend to multiple-family residential needs;</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">the property is not platted and there is no further development or change in land use; and</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">proximity to a public sewer arises from new construction initiated because of development other than on the premises concerned, and there is not otherwise determined to be a need for public sewer service to said premises.</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Availability is determined by the Wastewater Director, in the exercise of reasonable discretion.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Every owner, agent or occupant of any property constructing, using or maintaining an on-site sewage disposal system after public sewer service becomes available must discontinue use of the on-site facility and connect to the public system (POTW) upon the earliest of:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">the time the on-site system fails or requires pumping, or</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">within one year after public service became available or so long as deferred under subsection (D)(2) of this section.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 21</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0306">Section 13.03.0306</a> Proper Connection of All Premises<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Every owner, agent or occupant of any structure or premises used for human occupancy, employment, recreation or other purposes requiring sanitary facilities, or when the Wastewater Director or Health Officer shall so order, must construct or cause to be constructed all necessary sanitary facilities and a proper and sufficient sewer for connection to the public sewer in accordance with City requirements unless specifically exempted therefrom in writing by the Wastewater Director.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A separate and independent side sewer is provided for each and every building or structure or any premises or property, except as authorized by the Wastewater Director.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A private sewer may be permitted in cases of engineering necessity, to prevent or correct a health or safety hazard, or for other good cause, all as determined by the Wastewater Director or Health Officer.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Said side sewer connects said building, structure or property and all toilets and pipes therein used as receptacle of or conveyance of wastewater to the public sewer.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Upon discovery of a violation of this section, a notice of noncompliance is given to the owner, agent, or person in possession, charge or control of the premises which may allow up to thirty days for compliance.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A longer or shorter time may be set by the Wastewater Director or Health Officer as may be deemed necessary to protect the public health and safety.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No notice is required prior to or as a condition of taking any enforcement action.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 22</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0308">Section 13.03.0308</a> Easement – Agreement to Maintain Private Sewer<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">As an additional condition of allowing connection of a private sewer, the property owner may be required to execute and record at owner&rsquo;s expense an easement appurtenant to and for the benefit of premises crossed by a private sewer on a form supplied by the Development Services Center. A maintenance agreement must be filed with Spokane County.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Said easement is to be in a form approved by the City Attorney and recorded against all properties.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">It runs with the land and allows perpetual access to said private sewer by all premises crossed, to include all maintenance responsibilities shall be by property owners.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Grantors of property crossed mutually covenant to maintain said sewer for the use and enjoyment of all premises crossed or affected, as determined by the Director of Engineering Services.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Said easement is not subject to revocation without the written approval of the Director of Engineering Services.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The City has no maintenance or repair obligations for said private sewers.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 23</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0310">Section 13.03.0310</a> Multiple-dwelling Units – Duties of Owners and Occupants<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Every owner, agent and/or person in possession, charge or control of any hotel, motel, manufactured home park, condominium, apartment house or other multiple-dwelling unit arrangement has the duty to furnish such fixtures or other adequate means of disposing of wastewater originating from the premises as are approved by the Wastewater Director. This section is supplemental to authority which may be exercised by other City officials.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In cases of hotels, motels, manufactured home parks, condominiums, apartment houses, other multiple-dwelling unit arrangements or any other areas the Wastewater Director deems to require public sewer service, the Wastewater Director may require multiple tenants or the property owners to appoint an agent or agents responsible and accountable to the City for making payment for City sewer service whenever multiple billings are deemed unreliable or inconvenient.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Failure of an agent to discharge any duty imposed by this section does not relieve any property owner, tenant, occupant, customer or any other person of any legal obligation imposed herein and the City reserves all rights and remedies at contract and law.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 24</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0312">Section 13.03.0312</a> Disorders on Private Premises – Prompt Repairs<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">When any sewer, pipe, drain or on-site sewage disposal system located on private premises becomes obstructed, broken, out-of-order or otherwise inoperative, the Health Officer or the Wastewater Director, if the owner of such premises, customer, occupant or other person responsible for the care and management of the premises, or the agent of any of the foregoing (hereafter jointly and severally referenced as &ldquo;owner/customer&rdquo;) fails to correct the problem after two days&rsquo; notice to do so, and upon a determination that the public health and safety is or could be endangered thereby, causes such sewer to be removed, reconstructed, repaired, pumped, altered or cleansed, as deemed expedient, at the expense of the owner of such premises.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No notice is necessary in cases of imminent danger to the public health and safety.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Said broken, obstructed, out-of-order or otherwise inoperative sewers, pipes or on-site sewage disposal systems are declared public nuisances which may be summarily abated at the sole expense of the premises owner and/or responsible persons, notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In the case of a publicly owned sewer line, where the disorder was not the result of problems which have been determined by the Wastewater Director to have originated from an identifiable premises or area, the owner/customer is not responsible for repair expenses, but must allow prompt and reasonable access where required by the Wastewater Director on any abutting premises for repairs and maintenance as ordered by the Wastewater Director.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Property owner/customers are further required to cooperate with the Wastewater Director to allow the utility to repair or maintain the line or must pay any additional costs incurred by the utility because of failure to cooperate and allow access, which may be billed as a cost of sewer service to the premises concerned.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Cooperation includes providing access and information known to the owner/customer about any special conditions, underground obstructions or other information of any special problems relating to access or repair or maintenance activities.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">These obligations are supplemental to any other contractual undertaking or legal duty.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 25</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0314">Section 13.03.0314</a> Non-standard Strength Sewage – Special Arrangements<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Non-standard strength sewage must be made to conform to standard strength sewage consistent with the requirements of this chapter prior to discharge into the POTW at the generators or source&rsquo;s sole expense and liability.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Wastewater Director may, however, by special agreement or arrangement accept non-standard strength sewage subject to additional charges and terms as the Wastewater Director deems appropriate.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 26</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0316">Section 13.03.0316</a> Duty Imposed – Who is Responsible<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>Whenever this chapter imposes a duty on any identified person, party or permit holder, said duty or obligation is imposed on said person, party or permit holder’s successors in interest in addition but not by way of limitation.<br />&nbsp; 
        <li>When this chapter imposes a duty or prohibition upon a customer, user or other responsible party, said duty or prohibition applies in addition and not by way of limitation upon the owner, as defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=01.02.090">SMC 1.02.090</a>, of the realty upon which the wastewater source is located and upon all executive officers, managing agents and other persons in charge of the industrial or other facility generating the discharge.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0318">Section 13.03.0318</a> Unlawful to Dispose of Sewage<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Except as authorized by this chapter, no person may dispose of sewage, water-carried wastes or polluted waters.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Sanitary sewage is disposed of only into a sanitary or combined sewer with proper payment of all fees and charges therefor, or to an authorized on-site sewage disposal system.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Industrial process wastewater and non-contact cooling water is disposed of only into a sanitary or combined sewer, or other sewer or place approved by the Wastewater Director, with proper payment of all fees and charges therefor.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 27</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0320">Section 13.03.0320</a> Prohibited Uses of Sanitary Sewer<br />
        <p>No person may discharge or cause to be discharged any storm sewage into a sanitary sewer.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0322">Section 13.03.0322</a> Use of Storm Sewers, Combined Sewers, Natural Outlets<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Except as herein provided no person may discharge or cause to be discharged any wastewater, except stormwater, into a storm sewer. Additionally, notwithstanding the foregoing, non-contact cooling water or other wastewater (some unpolluted industrial process wastewaters) may be discharged upon approval of the City Engineer or Wastewater Director and the Washington State Department of Ecology to a storm sewer, combined sewer or natural outlet. Any such discharges may not cross over a public walk or&nbsp;way.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 28</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0324">Section 13.03.0324</a> Prohibited Uses of Public Sewers<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Absolute prohibited uses of a public sewer are stated in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.03.0406">SMC 13.03.0406</a>. In addition to these requirements, no person may directly or indirectly discharge or suffer or permit a discharge into any public sewer any of the following without previous written authorization from the Wastewater Director and payment of all required fees and charges therefor:</span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The contents of any tank or container owned or used by any person in the business of pumping, collecting, transporting or receiving sewage, effluent, septage or other waste substances, unless said person has obtained prior testing and written consent, as required by the Wastewater Director, and paid all fees assessed for such discharge; or</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Any non-standard strength sewage.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 29</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0326">Section 13.03.0326</a> Obstructing Sewer Prohibited<br />
        <p>No person may deposit any garbage, rubbish, dead animal or any substance having a tendency to obstruct the flow of the sewer in any sewer, access portal, manhole, lamphole, flush tank or sewer opening.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0328">Section 13.03.0328</a> Breaking Structures, Appurtenances Prohibited<br />
        <p>No person may break, damage, destroy, uncover, deface or tamper with any structure, appurtenance or equipment which is part of the POTW, including but not limited to, any portal, manhole, lamphole, catch basin, pump station, power source, supporting structures or substrate, or any part whatsoever or a public sewer.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 15, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, November 28, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34122 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0330">Section 13.03.0330</a> Unauthorized Connection to Public Sewer<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">No unauthorized person or entity may uncover, make any connection with, open into, use, alter, damage or disturb any public sewer or appurtenance thereof without first obtaining written permission from the Wastewater Director, obtaining permits as required by this code and Article VI of this chapter, and paying fees therefor.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 8, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 18, 2026</p><p>ORD C36776 Section 30</p>						<p>Article IV. Pretreatment</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0402">Section 13.03.0402</a> REPEALED (Objectives – Application)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0404">Section 13.03.0404</a> REPEALED (Prohibited Discharge Standards – General Prohibitions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0406">Section 13.03.0406</a> REPEALED (Prohibited Discharge Standards – Specific Prohibitions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0408">Section 13.03.0408</a> REPEALED (Prohibited Discharge Standards – Prevention – To Whom Applicable)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0410">Section 13.03.0410</a> REPEALED (Prohibited Discharge Standards – Affirmative Defenses)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0412">Section 13.03.0412</a> REPEALED (Categorical Pretreatment Standards)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0414">Section 13.03.0414</a> REPEALED (Categorical Violations – Upset Affirmative Defense)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0416">Section 13.03.0416</a> REPEALED (Local Limits)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0418">Section 13.03.0418</a> REPEALED (Level of Compliance Effort – Unreasonable Burden)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0420">Section 13.03.0420</a> REPEALED (Construction of Pretreatment Facilities)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0422">Section 13.03.0422</a> REPEALED (Side Sewer Manhole)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0424">Section 13.03.0424</a> REPEALED (Self-monitoring – City Inspections)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0426">Section 13.03.0426</a> REPEALED (Sampling and Analysis)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0428">Section 13.03.0428</a> REPEALED (Wastewater Discharge Permit Required)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0430">Section 13.03.0430</a> REPEALED (Times to Apply – New Permits, Renewals)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0432">Section 13.03.0432</a> REPEALED (Contents of Application)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0434">Section 13.03.0434</a> REPEALED (Confidentiality)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0436">Section 13.03.0436</a> REPEALED (Signing Permit Application, Reports, Other)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2008</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, November 23, 2008</p><p>ORD C34317 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=13.03.0438">Section 13.03.0438</a> REPEALED (Decision on Permit Application)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34317</p>
